WEBVTT

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.730
We will be heading toward Naha Airport as scheduled.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.360
Okinawa, huh?

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.730
It's been a while since I've been there.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.530
The "fasten seat belt" sign is off.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.660
However, for your safety, please do not leave your seat.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.950
The power of Thousand will only react to the pure Tera of the contractee.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.050
Excel-chan...

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.760
There is no meaning behind that kiss.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.050
Akane-san, you asked something quite interesting.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.510
Even though she said that...

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.270
Akane-san, what are you doing so suddenly?!

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.480
What's wrong? It's just for a while.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.860
It's not about time.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.400
It's weird for childhood friends to have their hands all over each other.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.660
And to think you were the one who wanted to hold hands in the past...

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.330
That was back when we were kids.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.750
Keita-kun, you were so cute back then.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.460
Akane-san, Kuro will look at us strangely.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.380
Kuro-chan is sound asleep.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.670
Miss!

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.970
This sandwich is free, right?

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.550
Right?

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.340
Y-Yes...

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.680
Can I have another one?

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.180
Can I eat three of them?

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.140
Erm, that's...

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.350
Can you give each of them two as well?

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.450
"The Hiba Clan"

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.370
Thanks for taking the long trip here from Tokyo.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.750
Welcome to Okinawa, Master Roots.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.340
I'm taking your picture.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.750
What's wrong?

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:07.810
We need your help this time with a high priority, top secret, Kaionji Group project.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.560
We're finally doing something befitting our statuses as Master Roots.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.110
Do you mind explaining what we're supposed to do?

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.360
A detailed meeting will be held during the welcome party later today.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.280
Hey, it has increased again.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.120
Yeah.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.370
More and more Tera is flowing toward this island.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.750
It's the same feeling as back then.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.880
That's right, a nasty feeling.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.760
Sorry, Punipuni.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.430
You're hungry, right?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.470
Here you go.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.270
Kuro, what's wrong?

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.600
Something is weird.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.140
There's an unusual amount of Tera here.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.400
What do you mean?

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.400
I don't really know... But it seems that a distorted power is involved.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.490
A distorted power?

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.950
Is this car okay?

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:03.410
It is.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.410
Hey, Keita-kun...

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.670
Will your grandfather be angry because we came here to visit him without calling ahead?

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.920
It'll be okay.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.250
Besides, he doesn't have a phone, so we can't contact him even if we wanted to.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.510
I'll go and get something.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.590
Well he would probably be okay with it if you were the only one visiting him.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.590
But Kuro-chan and I will be with you too...

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.140
He's not someone who would get worked up over such trivial things.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.930
Also, you've met him before, haven't you?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.440
Yes, but that was before I went to Tokyo.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.940
Anyway, be it investigating the photo or something else,

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:39.740
it's easier to do things if we use Grandpa's place as our base, I guess.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.110
I feel bad for relying on you for everything.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.910
It's okay... Don't worry about that.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.460
It's pretty!

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.790
The sea here is so shiny. It's completely different from Tokyo!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.670
Keita-san, why aren't you looking at it?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.090
I looked at it everyday when I was a kid.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.800
The sea is pretty much the only thing around here.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.550
You'll get sick of it after looking at it for another ten minutes.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:08.850
I won't get sick of it!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.850
Don't forget that we didn't come to Okinawa to play.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.480
Of course!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.270
We're here to find my brother and discover what happened to your moth—

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.990
Punipuni, why did you do that?!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.300
Grandpa!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.020
Hey, Grandpa!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.270
He's not in?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.980
He's probably out back.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.320
Out back?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.990
That's so cool!

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.620
Grandpa, long time no see.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.460
It's been a while.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.500
Oh, it's you, Keita?

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.460
Why did you come here out of the blue?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.170
I have some questions about that photo...

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.890
Maki?

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.810
It was taken here at Okinawa... Some time before Mother died...

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.770
Was Mother in Okinawa then?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.060
I don't think so.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.860
If the person in the photo really was Mother...

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.400
If it's really Maki?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.400
What do you mean?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.070
How should I say this...?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.410
It's called the Doppeliner system!

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.080
Doppel?

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.580
Hey, Kuro!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.080
What's wrong?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.670
Missy, are you Keita's friend?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.420
No, I'm not.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:08.430
I'm Kuro, a Mototsumitama.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.180
Keita-san is my contractee.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.100
Mototsumitama?

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.260
Yup!

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.270
Well then, I'll start by explaining the Doppeliner system!

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.730
No one will understand what you're saying because you're bringing it up so suddenly.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.190
But...

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:26.820
Anyway, we came here to investigate about Mother after we saw her on this photo.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:35.790
What a headache... I'm unable to explain what happened at Tokyo...

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.290
Well, I won't force an explanation out of you.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.790
Stay here as long as you want.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:49.050
The same goes for Akane-chan and this erm... Kuro-chan, right?

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.050
That's my name.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.800
What's wrong?

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.220
Thank you, Grandpa.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.930
Stop that, Keita.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.190
Don't bow to me.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.560
Anyway, you're in for a treat tonight.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.320
It just so happens that my neighbor gave me some nice meat.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.650
Wow, meat!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.450
Thank for the meal!

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:19.250
Want some of the Awamori that Keita bought for me?

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.000
You're old enough to drink, aren't you?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.630
No thanks. I'm not good with liquor.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.170
I see. What a pity.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.800
Thanks, Keita, it's pretty good.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.760
Grandpa, you've always liked to drink that, right?

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.890
Mind if I try a bit after all?

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.810
Here you go!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.990
Ah, you can hold your alcohol.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.530
No, I actually get drunk quite easily but it's not as if I hate drinking...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.660
Another cup, please!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.750
Are you okay? This is already your seventh cup.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.250
Fine, Sir!

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.180
Hey, Grandpa... Listen to me...

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.300
W-What's wrong?

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:19.010
You see... Even though Keita knows how I feel about him... He...

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.220
Thanks for the food.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.230
H-Hey, Keita!

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:26.270
Gosh, maybe I'll just get married to Grandpa!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.480
That was tasty.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.780
Keita-san?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.580
You can see a lot of stars from here.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.620
Stars?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.880
There really are a lot of them!

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.550
Keita-san, you somehow seem different from how you were before.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:00.180
Well, Excel did say that I've become somewhat good-looking...

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.520
Nope. You just seem more relaxed after you came here.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.520
Maybe, I guess.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.240
It's been a while since I've felt like this.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.620
Yeah.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:29.040
You can see clear water everywhere!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.460
Akane-san!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:33.670
Kuro-chan, you look cute!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.840
That sort of swimsuit really suits you.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.470
Thanks.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.640
Akane-san, you really do have a lot of  extraneous chest fat.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:48.690
Hey!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:50.980
Take this!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:51.940
What are you doing?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:54.730
Take that!

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.040
That was fun.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:10.750
Yeah!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.250
What's wrong?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.050
Keita-kun?

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:24.260
I was planning to find out where this photo was taken tomorrow.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.180
I see.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.600
Let's do that.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.730
Watch out!

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:33.980
This is...!

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.990
You know something about this photo?

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.650
Are you two Tribal Ends?!

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:42.410
No, they're Mototsumitama.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.240
What?!

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:53.000
We were tracking the presence of a great amount of Tera that led us here.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.340
As expected... You are probably after the Reiseki, aren't you?!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.840
Reiseki?!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.260
By Reiseki, do they mean what you told me the other day?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.260
Yes.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.800
There are others apart from the one in the pure land, and they protect the—

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.180
You are indeed with that bunch!

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.850
Keita-san!

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.940
Stop this!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.200
She really is a Mototsumitama!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:23.570
You two are the Mototsumitama of this land, right?

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.700
Why are you attacking us?

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.580
You're in cahoots with them, aren't you?!

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.710
You're after the Reiseki again, aren't you?!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.710
No! We're just—

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:33.920
Shut up!

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:41.090
Too slow!

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.260
She's weak!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:50.180
Yeah! She can't keep up with us!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.310
Kuro, your left!

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.770
Kuro!

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.070
Let's synchronize.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.610
I won't let you synchronize!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.910
Keita-kun!

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.910
There's no way you can win now!

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:08.580
Keita-san!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.410
An opening!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:10.910
Kuro...

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.710
I'm here!

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.170
I can't breathe...

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.430
If this goes on... Kuro and I will...

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:29.720
Don't forget this:

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:35.690
When a true crisis befalls a Mototsumitama, the contractee is the only one who can save her.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.440
That's right... I'm a contractee...

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.690
Kuro!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.710
What happened?!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.880
This is... the Thousand that Excel gave me...

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.680
Is this the power of a Thousand?

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.390
W-What happened?

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:17.650
Probably nothing more than a feint.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.900
Kuro, let's do it now!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:19.650
Okay!

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.920
Synchro!

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.300
Crap!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.970
Her Tera is gushing out!

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.840
Makana, don't be afraid!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:48.550
Too slow!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.430
Makana!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.230
I-I need to get some separation—

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.350
Crap!

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.350
Kakuma!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.940
Ouch...

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.210
Amazing...

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.500
She's too strong...

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.500
The two of you still want to continue?!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:30.010
Well then, can I have my photo back?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.390
Here.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.760
You know something about the photo, don't you?

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.020
Who are they?

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.190
What do you mean by "after the Reiseki?"

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.150
Hey, Makana, don't cry!

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.530
Sorry... Papa... Mama...

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.160
I was unable to protect the sacred precincts!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.160
Hush, don't cry. It's okay.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.160
We aren't your enemies.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.920
Reiseki.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:10.760
They are used to regulate the flow of Tera in an area and is the key item needed to maintain the balance of coexistence.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.680
The world is maintained by the Reiseki that is spread across the world.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:23.480
We, the Kaionji Group, aim to destroy these Reiseki and cause a temporary imbalance in the flow of Tera.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:31.200
We will use that Tera to create a world ruled by us, the Master Roots, and the Mototsumitama who support us.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.200
The world needs to be destroyed at least once.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:41.120
Human society has become depraved because the balance of coexistence has been maintained for too long.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.710
We must destroy the world

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:51.220
and create a new world for the Mototsumitama and the selected ones, the Master Roots.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:55.550
This will be the first time we destroy a Reiseki

00:15:56.100 --> 00:16:00.220
and it is a crucial milestone to our project.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.690
Even though the exact location of the Reiseki is still a mystery,

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:09.280
the Reiseki will start to respond to the large amount of Tera that we've gathered in this region.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:13.070
We've discovered a way to find the location based on this response.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:16.620
And that's why we, Master Roots, were gathered here?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:17.240
Yes.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:20.200
So it's okay for us to do anything we want to do?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:23.750
You can do anything as long as you remain in this hotel.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:29.630
You are free to use any of the facilities in this Kaionji resort.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:38.300
Because you were chosen, all you have to do is stay here.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:57.280
And so, they came to Okinawa seven years ago to find the Reiseki in the sacred precincts.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:05.620
After that, the people from the Shishigami clan killed the members of my clan since it was our task to guard that place.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.880
The Shishigami clan...

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:22.270
The Reiseki is essential to this region because it ensures that the Tera is flowing normally.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:28.520
To us, Mototsumitama, the Reiseki of where we live is more important than anything else.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.860
Everyone tried their best to fight...

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.070
But in the end, they got killed...

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:37.160
We're the only two who survived.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:38.530
That's why we made a vow.

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:42.040
We vowed that we would definitely protect the Reiseki and the sacred precincts!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.540
If this is really my mother...

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.920
Does it mean that Mother is responsible for exterminating their clan?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.470
Keita-kun?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:18:01.680
Anyway, it's a misunderstanding. We're not after your Reiseki.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.390
You're okay with this, right?

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:05.810
What's wrong?

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.270
You should know that we won't endanger you.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.650
That doesn't change the fact that this region is in danger!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:16.190
Even now, a large amount of Tera is continuing to gather in Okinawa!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:20.700
It seems that someone is purposely trying to upset the balance of the land here.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:24.040
They are definitely after the Reiseki!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:24.990
Let's head back!

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:26.200
Huh? But...

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.910
Please wait!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.460
It's too dangerous for the two of you to handle this!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.670
We've decided that just the two of us will protect the Reiseki.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.920
Let's go, Makana.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.720
Makana!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.300
O-Okay.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.720
They're quite stubborn.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.390
It's too dangerous.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.230
If my brother is the one after their Reiseki...

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:53.230
Okinawa isn't safe anymore as well?

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.950
Ibuki...

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.700
You came here after all.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:11.500
I've received it. Continue trailing them.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:13.750
Yeah.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:17.510
Just follow what the higher-ups say.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.220
Everything will start once the path to the Reiseki is opened up.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.600
Ibuki, I'm looking forward to it.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.480
To meeting with you again...

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.190
Amazing...

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.820
There's such a huge amount of Tera.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:43.820
It's worth looking forward to this, right, Shinobu?

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.490
Yes, it is.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:51.620
Please wait for me, Kuro-sama.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:56.210
This is the first frame of the ED

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:14.400
As it thaws my frozen body, before we realize it, dawn arrives.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:14.400
Itsu Shika Asa wo Mukae Itetsuku Karada Tokete

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:25.820
I've returned from my untimely death with my awakened memories.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:25.820
Sameta Kioku de Hayasugita Shi wo Kaeshite

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:38.210
The sounds of the bugs weeping, the sounds of the birds dancing in flight...

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:38.210
Mushitachi no Naku Koe mo Toritachi no Mau Haoto ni mo

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:54.600
This soundless, white wasteland will be overflowing with their vivid colors.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:54.600
Oto wo Nakushita Shiroki Kare Chi ni Afureru Iro wo Sosoide Iku Azayaka ni

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.570
This is the Kaionji Group's headquarters.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:01.690
It is our objective.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.110
Thanks for leading us here.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.860
Just leave the rest to us, the Noble One.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.700
H-Hold on! I'm going in, too!

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:14.870
This is my chance to exact my revenge from them for treating me like an experiment!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.580
There's no way that I'm missing this!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.750
Riona-san, things are not that simple.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.710
I'm going since I've already said so!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:23.380
I must have my revenge!

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.180
It looks like you suffered a lot, too.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.010
You sound like I'm making you suffer.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.060
Sorry.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:35.390
Come, let's go.

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:41.690
"Shadow of Mother"
